# Edge Function secrets: SERVER ONLY. Never in the app, never in mobile/.env*.
#
# Staging: copy this file to supabase/functions/.env.staging (gitignored), fill in what you need, then from mobile/:
#   npm run functions:secrets -- --env-file ../supabase/functions/.env.staging
# The path is relative to local-backend/, the Supabase CLI workdir every npm script uses.
# Local serving (optional): supabase/functions/.env, see supabase/functions/pet-talk/README.md.
#
# Lines stay commented unless you set them: an uncommented empty line would set an empty secret.
#
# Provided by the platform. Do not set them (the CLI refuses names that start with SUPABASE_):
#   SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pet-talk (the one function planned for staging)
# Required for real replies. Without it pet-talk answers configured:false and the app shows no "Talk" entry.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Model name. Default gpt-4o-mini until the owner picks one.
# OPENAI_MODEL=
# Per-user daily cap through consume_pet_chat_quota. Default 30.
# PET_TALK_MAX_PER_DAY=30
# Provider timeout in milliseconds. Default 20000.
# PET_TALK_TIMEOUT_MS=20000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pet-stylize (the painted portrait, from 1-3 photos)
# Required. The portrait is painted by a Gemini image model (docs/pet-portrait-v3.md).
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Image model. gemini-2.5-flash-image is the cheaper default; gemini-3-pro-image-preview paints noticeably finer
# fur and likeness (and costs several times more per portrait).
# GEMINI_IMAGE_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-image
# Output aspect ratio passed as imageConfig.aspectRatio (default 1:1). Set to an empty value to send no imageConfig.
# GEMINI_IMAGE_ASPECT=1:1
# Output size hint ("1K", "2K" or "4K"). Only Gemini 3 Pro Image understands it; leave unset for 2.5 Flash Image.
# GEMINI_IMAGE_SIZE=
# How long one painting call may take, in milliseconds. Default 60000.
# GEMINI_IMAGE_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
# imageUrl (the "paint again" path) may only point at this project's storage host. Extra hosts, comma-separated:
# PET_STYLIZE_ALLOWED_IMAGE_HOSTS=
# Model for background removal; defaults to GEMINI_IMAGE_MODEL.
# GEMINI_BG_REMOVAL_MODEL=
# Optional external background-removal service.
# BACKGROUND_REMOVAL_URL=
# BACKGROUND_REMOVAL_API_KEY=
# An extra "Name: value" header for that service (the key is also sent as Authorization: Bearer <key>).
# BACKGROUND_REMOVAL_AUTH_HEADER=
# auto (default), gemini_nano or removebg.
# BACKGROUND_REMOVAL_PROVIDER=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pet-chat, weekly-summary (retired; do NOT deploy)
# Listed so every variable the code reads is documented (docs/backend/STAGING_PLAN.md section 2.4).
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openrouter/free
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant
# PROVIDER_PRIMARY=openrouter
# PROVIDER_FALLBACK=groq
# MAX_REQ_PER_DAY=
# REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=
# PET_CHAT_ALLOW_FALLBACK_REPLY=false
# WEEKLY_SUMMARY_ADMIN_SECRET=
